        <briefdescription>
<para>This method is called during prolog/epilog code insertion to eliminate call frame setup and destroy pseudo instructions (but only if the <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_target" kindref="compound">Target</ref> is using them). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>It is responsible for eliminating these instructions, replacing them with concrete instructions. This method need only be implemented if using call frame setup/destroy pseudo instructions. Returns an iterator pointing to the instruction after the replaced one. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
