        <definition>void LanaiFrameLowering::determineCalleeSaves</definition>
        <argsstring>(MachineFunction &amp;MF, BitVector &amp;SavedRegs, RegScavenger *RS=nullptr) const override</argsstring>
        <name>determineCalleeSaves</name>
        <qualifiedname>llvm::LanaiFrameLowering::determineCalleeSaves</qualifiedname>
        <reimplements refid="classllvm_1_1_target_frame_lowering_1a2f26766f4dcfa6457ba405584a34d5c3">determineCalleeSaves</reimplements>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_machine_function" kindref="compound">MachineFunction</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>MF</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_bit_vector" kindref="compound">BitVector</ref> &amp;</type>
          <declname>SavedRegs</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type><ref refid="classllvm_1_1_reg_scavenger" kindref="compound">RegScavenger</ref> *</type>
          <declname>RS</declname>
          <defval>nullptr</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This method determines which of the registers reported by <ref refid="classllvm_1_1_target_register_info_1ad71b5bc0aa81f5dec06cbfecaf2f7183" kindref="member">TargetRegisterInfo::getCalleeSavedRegs()</ref> should actually get saved. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>The default implementation checks populates the <computeroutput>SavedRegs</computeroutput> bitset with all registers which are modified in the function, targets may override this function to save additional registers. This method also sets up the register scavenger ensuring there is a free register or a frameindex available. This method should not be called by any passes outside of PEI, because it may change state passed in by <computeroutput>MF</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>RS</computeroutput>. The preferred interface outside PEI is getCalleeSaves. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
